---
<GuideLayout title="Dolls | L2 Guardian Guides" lang="en" active="dolls" toc={toc}>
<div class="content">
  <a class="back" href="/en/">← Back to home</a>
  <section class="hero">
    <img src="/images/dolls-collections.png" alt="Doll collections in L2 Reborn Guardian"/>
    <div class="hero-body"><div class="badge">GUARDIAN SYSTEM</div><h1>Dolls</h1><p class="subtitle">A permanent passive progression system built around summoning Dolls, using duplicates in Compound and completing Collections.</p>
      <div class="info-grid"><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Chapter 1 Rarities</div><div class="value">Common + Enhanced</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Weekly Purge Drop</div><div class="value">10% Selection</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Weekly Purge Drop</div><div class="value">20% Summon</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Compound Cost</div><div class="value">From 100k</div></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section quick-start"><div class="quick-head"><div class="quick-icon">🧸</div><div><h2>Quick Start</h2><p>The essential rules of the Doll system.</p></div></div>
    <div class="quick-grid"><div class="quick-card"><div class="quick-title">Main Source</div><div class="quick-value">Weekly Purges</div><span class="quick-tag high">Use Every Key</span></div><div class="quick-card"><div class="quick-title">Passive Bonuses</div><div class="quick-value">Always Active</div><span class="quick-tag high">No Equip Needed</span></div><div class="quick-card"><div class="quick-title">Compound</div><div class="quick-value">4 Duplicates</div><span class="quick-tag medium">Chance to Upgrade Tier</span></div><div class="quick-card"><div class="quick-title">Early Priority</div><div class="quick-value">Flat Stats</div><span class="quick-tag high">Best Early Value</span></div></div>
    <div class="quick-footer"><div class="quick-tip"><strong>Physical characters</strong>Save five Selection Common Doll Coupons and target Lilith Doll.</div><div class="quick-tip"><strong>Magical characters</strong>Save five Selection Common Doll Coupons and target Anakim Doll.</div><div class="quick-tip"><strong>Higher rarity replaces lower</strong>Only the best owned version of the same Doll applies its personal stats.</div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="overview"><h2>Overview</h2><p>Dolls are permanent passive character upgrades. Every owned Doll provides its listed statistics automatically. There is no need to summon it into the world, equip it or choose an active preset.</p><p>Different Dolls support different builds. Some provide physical statistics such as P. Atk., while others provide magical statistics such as M. Atk. Collections add further bonuses for owning specific groups of Dolls.</p><div class="note"><strong>Important:</strong> The word Summon refers to obtaining a Doll. Dolls are not active pets and their bonuses remain in effect automatically.</div></section>

  <section class="section" id="access"><h2>How to Access Dolls</h2><div class="steps"><div class="step"><div class="num">1</div><div><strong>Open the main menu</strong><p>Use the Menu button in the lower right corner of the game interface.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">2</div><div><strong>Select Dolls</strong><p>Click Dolls in the upper left area of the main menu.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">3</div><div><strong>Choose a system tab</strong><p>The window contains Dolls, Summon, Compounding, Enhancement and Collections. Enhancement is not currently available.</p></div></div></div><div class="guide-gallery wide"><figure><img src="/images/dolls-menu.png" alt="Opening Dolls from the main menu"/><figcaption>Open the lower right menu and select Dolls.</figcaption></figure></div></section>

  <section class="section" id="obtaining"><h2>How to Obtain Dolls</h2><p>Doll coupons are obtained through weekly Purges in farming zones. Each key used during a Purge has its own chance to award one of the following items:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Reward</th><th>Chance per Key</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Doll Selection Coupon</td><td class="good">10%</td><td>Choose a specific available Common Doll by paying its listed coupon cost.</td></tr><tr><td>Doll Summon Coupon</td><td class="good">20%</td><td>Receive a random Doll from the coupon's summon pool.</td></tr></tbody></table></section>

  <section class="section" id="summoning"><h2>Summoning Dolls</h2><h3>Using a Doll Summon Coupon</h3><p>Use the right mouse button on a Common Doll Summon Coupon in the inventory. In the window that opens, click <strong>Summon result</strong> or select the displayed card to reveal the random Doll.</p><h3>Using Selection Common Doll Coupons</h3><p>Use a Selection Common Doll Coupon to open its exchange list. These coupons can only select Common Dolls. Each Common Doll has its own price, so some choices require more coupons than others. Enhanced Dolls cannot be selected during Chapter 1.</p><h3>Summoning with Adena</h3><p>The Summon tab in the Dolls window also offers unlimited Adena summons. One summon costs 1,000,000 Adena and eleven summons cost 11,000,000 Adena. Use <strong>Summon List</strong> to inspect the current reward pool and the individual probability of every Doll before spending.</p><div class="guide-gallery"><figure><img src="/images/dolls-coupon-summon.png" alt="Using a Common Doll Summon Coupon"/><figcaption>Reveal the random result supplied by a Summon Coupon.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/images/dolls-selection-exchange.png" alt="Exchanging Selection Common Doll Coupons"/><figcaption>Selection prices vary between Common Dolls.</figcaption></figure></div><div class="guide-gallery wide"><figure><img src="/images/dolls-adena-summon.png" alt="Doll summons with Adena and the Summon List"/><figcaption>The probability list is available directly from the Summon tab.</figcaption></figure></div><div class="warning"><strong>Check the rates first.</strong> Adena summons have no limit and can consume a large amount of currency very quickly.</div></section>

  <section class="section" id="rarities"><h2>Rarities and Passive Stats</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Rarity</th><th>Color</th><th>Guardian Availability</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Common</td><td>Gray</td><td class="good">Available in Chapter 1</td></tr><tr><td>Enhanced</td><td>Green</td><td class="good">Available in Chapter 1 through Summon or Compound</td></tr><tr><td>Superior</td><td>Orange</td><td>Unlocks in Chapter 2</td></tr></tbody></table><p>All owned Doll statistics are passive and always active. However, two rarities of the same Doll do not stack their personal bonuses. Only the highest rarity owned remains active.</p><div class="example"><strong>Example: Princess Molrang</strong><p>The Common version provides Speed +1 and the Enhanced version provides Speed +2. If both are owned, the character receives Speed +2, not Speed +3.</p></div><p>This replacement rule only affects different versions of the same Doll. Other owned Dolls continue providing their own passive statistics normally.</p></section>

  <section class="section" id="compound"><h2>Compounding Duplicate Dolls</h2><p>Compound converts duplicate Dolls into a new random Doll. Only duplicates appear as available materials. You need four duplicate Dolls of the same rarity, but the Adena fee depends on their tier.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Material Tier</th><th>Dolls Required</th><th>Adena Cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Common</td><td>4 duplicates</td><td>100,000</td></tr><tr><td>Enhanced</td><td>4 duplicates</td><td>500,000</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="steps"><div class="step"><div class="num">1</div><div><strong>Select one rarity</strong><p>All four material Dolls must belong to the same rarity, but they do not need to be four copies of the same named Doll.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">2</div><div><strong>Add four duplicates</strong><p>Only duplicate Dolls are shown as available for Compound. The four selected copies and the corresponding Adena fee are consumed.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">3</div><div><strong>Receive one random Doll</strong><p>You always receive one Doll from the probability list. The result can have the same rarity or a higher rarity.</p></div></div></div><p>A same rarity result is often called a failure, but it may still unlock a Doll you do not own. A higher rarity result is the successful upgrade outcome. Open <strong>Rate Check</strong> to see the exact possible Dolls and their current chances.</p><div class="guide-gallery wide"><figure><img src="/images/dolls-compound.png" alt="Doll Compounding and its probability list"/><figcaption>Four duplicate Dolls are exchanged for one random result from the displayed list.</figcaption></figure></div><div class="note"><strong>Collection progress still counts:</strong> Dolls obtained through Compound can complete Collections and activate statistics exactly like Dolls obtained from any other source.</div></section>

  <section class="section" id="collections"><h2>Doll Collections</h2><p>The Collections tab displays groups of specific Dolls. Owning every required Doll completes the group and automatically activates its additional statistics. Collections can be filtered by Attack, Defense, Battle Assist or Stats, and the search field can locate collections containing a specific Doll.</p><p>Collection bonuses are separate from each Doll's personal passive statistics. Completing a Collection therefore adds another permanent source of character progression.</p><div class="guide-gallery wide"><figure><img src="/images/dolls-collections.png" alt="Completed and incomplete Doll Collections"/><figcaption>Green check marks identify completed Collections and their active bonuses.</figcaption></figure></div></section>

  <section class="section" id="strategy"><h2>Recommended Progression</h2><div class="steps"><div class="step"><div class="num">1</div><div><strong>Prioritize flat statistics early</strong><p>During the early stages of a server, fixed increases such as P. Atk. or M. Atk. commonly provide more practical value than small percentage bonuses.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">2</div><div><strong>Match Dolls to your character</strong><p>Physical characters should prioritize physical bonuses. Magical characters should prioritize magical bonuses.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">3</div><div><strong>Save Selection Coupons for a strong target</strong><p>Keep five Selection Common Doll Coupons. Physical characters should target Lilith Doll, while magical characters should target Anakim Doll.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">4</div><div><strong>Use duplicates in Compound</strong><p>Only duplicate Dolls appear as available materials in the Compound window.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">5</div><div><strong>Review Collections before selecting</strong><p>A Doll that looks less useful by itself may complete a Collection and provide a valuable account goal.</p></div></div></div></section>

  <section class="section" id="future"><h2>Chapter 2 and Future Content</h2><p>During Chapter 1, Purges provide Common Dolls and Enhanced Dolls are mainly obtained through random summoning or Compound. In Chapter 2, Enhanced Dolls replace Common Dolls in Purge rewards and the orange Superior rarity becomes available.</p><p>The Enhancement tab visible in the Dolls window is not currently active and belongs to future content.</p><div class="warning"><strong>Not available yet:</strong> Do not plan current progression around Doll Enhancement or Superior Dolls until Chapter 2 content is enabled.</div></section>

  <section class="section" id="mistakes"><h2>Common Mistakes</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>Why It Hurts</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spending Selection Coupons immediately</td><td>You may delay a targeted Lilith or Anakim Doll that needs five coupons.</td></tr><tr><td>Expecting two rarities of one Doll to stack</td><td>Only the highest owned rarity applies that Doll's personal statistics.</td></tr><tr><td>Using unlimited Adena summons without checking rates</td><td class="bad">The system can consume large amounts of Adena without guaranteeing your desired Doll.</td></tr><tr><td>Ignoring Collections</td><td>You may overlook permanent bonuses or use duplicates without considering collection goals.</td></tr><tr><td>Thinking a same rarity Compound result is worthless</td><td>The result may be a new Doll that provides passive stats or completes a Collection.</td></tr></tbody></table></section>
</div>
</GuideLayout>
